1
00:01:17,370 --> 00:01:20,910
I got nothing, sir. 
No sign of Niobe or Ghost.

2
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:22,620
Nothing but blue pills.

3
00:01:22,750 --> 00:01:24,460
Should we try to contact them?

4
00:01:24,630 --> 00:01:26,590
Won't matter. 
My gut says they're down.

5
00:01:26,750 --> 00:01:29,800
- We should start back. 
- If that ship can fly, we need it.

6
00:01:30,050 --> 00:01:31,470
I was afraid you'd say that.

7
00:01:31,630 --> 00:01:34,300
Search every pipe, every hole, 
every crack we know.

8
00:01:34,470 --> 00:01:36,930
Sweep as wide as possible, 
as fast as possible.

9
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:40,810
- Lines are crawling with calamari. 
- Then the sooner we find them the better.

10
00:01:47,270 --> 00:01:48,980
Thought you could use 
something to eat.

11
00:01:49,110 --> 00:01:50,820
Thank you.

12
00:01:51,150 --> 00:01:53,530
Any change?

13
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:56,410
No.

14
00:01:57,490 --> 00:02:01,330
- How is he? 
- He's gonna be fine.

15
00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:04,120
At least until he wakes up.

16
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:08,460
- What do you mean? 
- Captain has some questions for him.

17
00:02:08,630 --> 00:02:09,880
He'd better have some good answers.

18
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:14,130
You see these cuts? 
I think they're self-inflicted.

19
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:18,350
- Why? 
- VDTs maybe. I don't know.

20
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:21,850
But like I said, 
the answer better be good.

21
00:02:24,810 --> 00:02:28,190
Roland, I'd like to run 
another search through the Matrix.

22
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:30,570
- For what? 
- For Neo.

23
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:33,990
How could he be in the Matrix, sir? 
He's not plugged in.

24
00:02:34,150 --> 00:02:35,490
Please, for me.

25
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:48,710
This is what keeps bothering me.

26
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:50,880
What?

27
00:02:51,630 --> 00:02:54,720
His neural patterns don't read 
like someone who's in a coma.

28
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:57,840
The strange thing is, 
I see these patterns all the time.

29
00:02:58,010 --> 00:03:01,350
- Where? 
- On someone jacked in.

30
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:16,320
The big <i>bupkes. Nada.</i> 
He's not in there.

31
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:18,740
- Sir, I got the projections. 
- How long?

32
00:03:18,910 --> 00:03:23,410
Based on point of entry and past speed, 
the machines will be in Zion in 20 hours.

33
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:26,250
Jesus H. Christ.

34
00:03:26,910 --> 00:03:31,040
All right, let's move with a purpose. 
AK, I want you on holographics.

35
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:34,340
Mauser, I want forward and aft guns 
manned at all times.

36
00:03:34,550 --> 00:03:36,630
Make sure we're running 
on as few pads as possible.

37
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:38,680
- Yes, sir. 
- Hey.

38
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:41,970
- Hey! You got a call. 
- What?

39
00:03:43,390 --> 00:03:45,560
Operator.

40
00:03:45,850 --> 00:03:48,270
It's Seraph.

41
00:03:49,230 --> 00:03:52,690
I bring word from the Oracle. 
You must come at once.

42
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:10,170
- Where am I? 
- This is the train station.

43
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:16,250
- This isn't the Matrix? 
- That's where the train goes.

44
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:19,720
That's where we're going, 
but you cannot go with us.

45
00:04:20,930 --> 00:04:23,890
- Why not? 
- He won't let you.

46
00:04:24,890 --> 00:04:28,600
- Who won't? 
- The Trainman. I don't like him.

47
00:04:28,770 --> 00:04:32,100
But my papa says we have to do 
what the Trainman says...

48
00:04:32,270 --> 00:04:36,150
...or else he will leave us here 
forever and ever.

49
00:04:50,750 --> 00:04:55,420
Morpheus, Trinity, 
thank you for coming.

50
00:04:56,130 --> 00:04:58,340
One thing I've learned in all my years...

51
00:04:58,550 --> 00:05:01,630
...is that nothing ever works out 
the way you want it to.

52
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:04,850
- Who are you? 
- I'm the Oracle.

53
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:11,850
I wish there was an easy way to get 
through this, but there ain't.

54
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:14,940
I'm sorry this had to happen.

55
00:05:15,110 --> 00:05:18,650
I'm sorry I couldn't be sitting here 
like you remember me...

56
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:21,780
- ...but it wasn't meant to be. 
- What happened?

57
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:26,870
I made a choice, and that choice 
cost me more than I wanted it to.

58
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:28,450
What choice?

59
00:05:28,910 --> 00:05:31,710
To help you, to guide Neo.

60
00:05:31,910 --> 00:05:36,840
Now, since the real test for any choice is 
having to make the same choice again...

61
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,800
...knowing full well 
what it might cost...

62
00:05:41,010 --> 00:05:43,550
...I guess I feel pretty good 
about that choice...

63
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:48,010
...because here I am, at it again.

64
00:05:48,310 --> 00:05:52,060
- Do you know what happened to Neo? 
- Yes.

65
00:05:52,430 --> 00:05:56,980
He is trapped in a place between 
this world and the machine world.

66
00:05:57,310 --> 00:06:01,490
The link is controlled by a program 
called the Trainman.

67
00:06:01,650 --> 00:06:06,160
He uses it to smuggle programs 
in and out of the Matrix.

68
00:06:06,370 --> 00:06:09,530
If he finds out where Neo is 
before you get to him...

69
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:13,160
...then I'm afraid our choices 
are going to become difficult.

70
00:06:13,330 --> 00:06:16,500
- Why? 
- Because of who the Trainman works for.

71
00:06:16,670 --> 00:06:18,500
The Merovingian.

72
00:06:18,710 --> 00:06:23,220
He has placed a bounty on your lives. 
You must be careful at all times.

73
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:27,930
Seraph knows how to find the Trainman. 
He'll go with you.

74
00:06:28,220 --> 00:06:31,890
For years he has protected me.

75
00:06:32,060 --> 00:06:34,560
I hope he can do the same for you.

76
00:06:35,690 --> 00:06:38,400
Please, follow me.

77
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:45,030
Oracle...

78
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:47,410
I know, Morpheus.

79
00:06:47,570 --> 00:06:51,280
I can see you're filled with doubt, 
clouded by uncertainty.

80
00:06:51,490 --> 00:06:56,080
After everything that has happened, 
how can you expect me to believe you?

81
00:06:56,250 --> 00:06:58,000
I don't.

82
00:06:58,210 --> 00:07:00,880
I expect just what I've always expected:

83
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:05,300
For you to make up your own 
damn mind. Believe me or don't.

84
00:07:05,510 --> 00:07:10,890
All I can do is tell you that your friend 
is in trouble, and he needs your help.

85
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:14,470
He needs all our help.

86
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:17,600
- Are you from the Matrix? 
- Yes.

87
00:07:17,730 --> 00:07:19,100
No.

88
00:07:19,270 --> 00:07:23,150
- I mean, I was. 
- Why did you leave?

89
00:07:24,070 --> 00:07:27,320
- I had to. 
- I had to leave my home too.

90
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:31,280
Sati! Come here, darling. 
Leave the poor man in peace.

91
00:07:31,450 --> 00:07:32,950
Yes, Papa.

92
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:41,460
I am sorry. She is still very curious.

93
00:07:41,960 --> 00:07:45,420
- I know you. 
- Yes, in the restaurant of the Frenchman.

94
00:07:45,590 --> 00:07:50,300
I am Rama-Kandra. This is my wife, 
Kamala. My daughter, Sati.

95
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:52,470
We are most honored to meet you.

96
00:07:53,050 --> 00:07:55,270
- You are programs. 
- Oh, yes.

97
00:07:55,810 --> 00:07:59,850
I am the power-plant systems manager 
for recycling operations.

98
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:04,110
My wife is an interactive software 
programmer. She is highly creative.

99
00:08:04,320 --> 00:08:06,780
What are you doing here? 
You do not belong here.

100
00:08:06,990 --> 00:08:11,870
Kamala! Goodness, I apologize. 
My wife can be very direct.

101
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:14,660
It's okay.

102
00:08:14,990 --> 00:08:16,500
I don't have an answer.

103
00:08:16,660 --> 00:08:20,170
- I don't even know where "here" is. 
- This place is nowhere.

104
00:08:20,580 --> 00:08:23,130
It is between your world and our world.

105
00:08:24,670 --> 00:08:27,670
- Who's the Trainman? 
- He works for the Frenchman.

106
00:08:28,130 --> 00:08:30,010
Why did I know 
you were going to say that?

107
00:08:30,180 --> 00:08:34,140
The Frenchman does not forget, 
and he does not forgive.

108
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:37,180
- You know him? 
- I know only what I need to know.

109
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:41,350
I know if you want to take something 
from our world into your world...

110
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:44,730
...that does not belong there, 
you must go to the Frenchman.

111
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:46,530
Is that what you're doing here?

112
00:08:46,690 --> 00:08:50,700
- Rama, please. 
- I do not want to be cruel, Kamala.

113
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:53,410
He may never see another face 
for the rest of his life.

114
00:08:53,870 --> 00:08:55,660
I'm sorry.

115
00:08:55,830 --> 00:08:59,080
- You don't have to answer that question. 
- No, I don't mind.

116
00:08:59,700 --> 00:09:02,040
The answer is simple.

117
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:10,010
I love my daughter very much.

118
00:09:10,170 --> 00:09:13,680
I find her to be the most beautiful thing 
I have ever seen.

119
00:09:13,890 --> 00:09:16,550
But where we are from, 
that is not enough.

120
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:19,390
Every program that is created 
must have a purpose.

121
00:09:19,640 --> 00:09:22,940
If it does not, it is deleted.

122
00:09:23,140 --> 00:09:26,770
I went to the Frenchman 
to save my daughter.

123
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:31,740
- You do not understand. 
- I just have never...

124
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:34,240
Heard a program speak of love.

125
00:09:35,030 --> 00:09:38,490
- It is a human emotion. 
- No, it is a word.

126
00:09:39,540 --> 00:09:43,920
What matters is the connection 
the word implies.

127
00:09:46,380 --> 00:09:49,340
I see that you are in love.

128
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:53,930
Can you tell me what you would give 
to hold on to that connection?

129
00:09:54,090 --> 00:09:55,430
Anything.

130
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:57,600
Then perhaps the reason you are here...

131
00:09:57,760 --> 00:10:01,060
...is not so different 
than the reason I am here.

132
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:10,650
That's him.

133
00:10:11,780 --> 00:10:14,650
- Get away! Get away from me! 
- We don't want trouble.

134
00:10:14,860 --> 00:10:17,780
- Get the hell away from me! 
- We need your help.

135
00:10:17,910 --> 00:10:21,490
I can't help you! 
No one can help you!

136
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:14,010
Oh, no!

137
00:11:26,350 --> 00:11:27,940
Damn it!

138
00:11:31,020 --> 00:11:35,030
- When is the train due? 
- It is already late.

139
00:11:35,190 --> 00:11:37,360
It's not like the Trainman to be late.

140
00:11:37,990 --> 00:11:40,030
You think it has something 
to do with me?

141
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:41,530
I cannot say.

142
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:44,540
Who knows such things? 
Only the Oracle.

143
00:11:44,700 --> 00:11:47,540
- You know the Oracle? 
- Everyone knows the Oracle.

144
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:50,500
I consulted with her 
before I met with the Frenchman.

145
00:11:50,670 --> 00:11:53,210
She promised she'd look after Sati 
after we said goodbye.

146
00:11:53,340 --> 00:11:55,380
Goodbye?

147
00:11:55,550 --> 00:11:58,220
- You're not staying with her? 
- It is not possible.

148
00:11:58,380 --> 00:12:02,390
Our arrangement with the Frenchman 
was for our daughter only.

149
00:12:02,550 --> 00:12:06,060
- My wife and I must return to our world. 
- Why?

150
00:12:06,350 --> 00:12:09,230
- That is our karma. 
- You believe in karma?

151
00:12:09,390 --> 00:12:12,610
Karma is a word, like love.

152
00:12:12,810 --> 00:12:14,570
A way of saying:

153
00:12:14,820 --> 00:12:17,030
"What I am here to do."

154
00:12:17,190 --> 00:12:20,780
I do not resent my karma. 
I'm grateful for it.

155
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:24,410
Grateful for my wonderful wife, 
for my beautiful daughter.

156
00:12:24,580 --> 00:12:28,750
They are gifts, and so I do 
what I must do to honor them.

157
00:12:30,330 --> 00:12:33,750
- Papa, the train! 
- Yes. Find your bag. Quickly.

158
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:38,760
Can I carry that for you?

159
00:12:39,920 --> 00:12:41,930
All right.

160
00:12:47,350 --> 00:12:48,640
Hurry it up, I'm late!

161
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:55,060
Who are you?

162
00:12:55,270 --> 00:12:56,980
- He is a friend. 
- Rama!

163
00:12:57,860 --> 00:13:00,610
I know you.

164
00:13:00,740 --> 00:13:04,450
- So that's what they wanted. 
- I need to get back.

165
00:13:05,620 --> 00:13:07,990
- I'll pay you whatever you want. 
- Oh.

166
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:10,620
One way or another, 
I'm getting on this train.

167
00:13:10,870 --> 00:13:12,500
Oh, no, no, no.

168
00:13:12,710 --> 00:13:15,630
You'll stay right here until 
the Merovingian says different.

169
00:13:15,790 --> 00:13:17,300
If I know him...

170
00:13:17,460 --> 00:13:20,970
...you're gonna be here 
for a long, long time.

171
00:13:21,380 --> 00:13:25,180
- I don't want to hurt you. 
- You don't get it.

172
00:13:25,390 --> 00:13:27,970
I built this place.

173
00:13:28,100 --> 00:13:32,480
Down here, I make the rules. 
Down here, I make the threats.

174
00:13:39,650 --> 00:13:43,360
Get on the train 
or you'll stay here with him.

175
00:13:59,210 --> 00:14:02,130
We should return to the Oracle. 
She will know what to do.

176
00:14:02,340 --> 00:14:05,090
No. We know what has to be done.

177
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:22,150
Shit.

178
00:14:50,470 --> 00:14:52,930
You gotta be kidding.

179
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:55,140
Holy shit, it's wingless.

180
00:14:55,940 --> 00:14:57,480
I get it.

181
00:14:57,600 --> 00:15:00,480
You must be ready to die.

182
00:15:00,770 --> 00:15:02,320
I need to speak with him.

183
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:07,110
Only way you're getting through 
this door is over my big, dead ass.

184
00:15:07,950 --> 00:15:09,280
So be it.

185
00:15:32,510 --> 00:15:34,890
There are no weapons allowed 
in the club.

186
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:38,520
At the bottom of this elevator, 
there is a coat-check girl...

187
00:15:38,690 --> 00:15:41,860
...and if we are lucky, 
one man for checking weapons.

188
00:15:42,360 --> 00:15:44,190
And if we're unlucky?

189
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:46,240
There will be many men.

190
00:15:48,030 --> 00:15:50,740
Can I take your...? Oh, my God.

191
00:18:12,510 --> 00:18:15,010
What in the hell?

192
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:19,560
I don't believe this.

193
00:18:25,520 --> 00:18:28,400
Hey! Hey!

194
00:18:31,190 --> 00:18:34,150
The prodigal child returns.

195
00:18:36,780 --> 00:18:40,410
Are you here for the bounty, Seraph?

196
00:18:42,500 --> 00:18:45,370
Tell me, how many bullets 
are there in those guns?

197
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:48,710
I don't know, but I don't think 
you have enough.

198
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:51,710
- We only want to talk. 
- Oh, yes.

199
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:57,220
I'm sure you do. You have fought 
through Hel to do so. Yes?

200
00:18:57,640 --> 00:18:59,600
I'll tell you what I will do.

201
00:18:59,800 --> 00:19:03,720
Put down the guns, and I will promise 
you a safe passage out of here.

202
00:19:04,140 --> 00:19:06,560
- All three of us? 
- Oh, yes, yes.

203
00:19:07,650 --> 00:19:09,440
Of course.

204
00:19:35,510 --> 00:19:41,260
Who could have guessed we'd see each 
other so soon after our last meeting?

205
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:44,470
The Fates are too kind, eh?

206
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:48,140
And since you, my little Judas, 
have brought them here...

207
00:19:48,350 --> 00:19:53,150
...I can only surmise the fortuneteller 
has found herself another shell?

208
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:56,610
Disappointing, but not unexpected.

209
00:19:56,780 --> 00:20:00,280
I do hope, however, she has the good 
manners to learn her lesson...

210
00:20:00,450 --> 00:20:03,740
...and to remember that there is 
no action without consequence.

211
00:20:03,950 --> 00:20:08,080
And if you take something from me, 
you will pay the price.

212
00:20:09,210 --> 00:20:12,000
You know why we are here?

213
00:20:12,630 --> 00:20:15,800
Come now, what kind of question 
is this? Of course I know.

214
00:20:15,960 --> 00:20:18,010
It is my business to know.

215
00:20:18,220 --> 00:20:21,470
Some might think this is a strange 
coincidence, but I do not.

216
00:20:21,890 --> 00:20:28,140
I am curious, though, 
as to how it actually happened.

217
00:20:28,310 --> 00:20:30,480
- Do you know? 
- No.

218
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:32,360
No?

219
00:20:32,560 --> 00:20:34,690
I did not think so.

220
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:37,820
But it is always best to ask, huh?

221
00:20:37,940 --> 00:20:40,030
We want to make a deal.

222
00:20:41,570 --> 00:20:45,990
Always straight to business, 
huh, Morpheus?

223
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:50,500
Okay. I have something you want.

224
00:20:50,670 --> 00:20:52,670
To make a deal...

225
00:20:52,830 --> 00:20:58,340
...you must have something 
I want, yes?

226
00:20:58,590 --> 00:21:02,840
And it so happens 
there is something I want.

227
00:21:03,010 --> 00:21:07,350
Something I have wanted 
ever since I first came here.

228
00:21:07,600 --> 00:21:10,350
It is said they cannot be taken...

229
00:21:10,770 --> 00:21:13,060
...they can only be given.

230
00:21:13,270 --> 00:21:14,560
What?

231
00:21:17,110 --> 00:21:19,570
The eyes of the Oracle.

232
00:21:23,360 --> 00:21:26,910
I told you before, there is no escaping 
the nature of the universe.

233
00:21:27,120 --> 00:21:29,870
It is that nature 
that has again brought you to me.

234
00:21:30,040 --> 00:21:33,710
Where some see coincidence, 
I see consequence.

235
00:21:33,830 --> 00:21:36,170
Where others see chance...

236
00:21:36,340 --> 00:21:39,880
...I see cost.

237
00:21:42,050 --> 00:21:45,340
Bring me the eyes of the Oracle...

238
00:21:45,850 --> 00:21:48,760
...and I will give you back your savior.

239
00:21:49,390 --> 00:21:53,730
It seems a perfectly fair 
and reasonable deal to me.

240
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:55,770
Yes? No?

241
00:21:58,230 --> 00:21:59,940
I don't have time for this shit.

242
00:22:31,770 --> 00:22:34,440
You wanna make a deal? 
How about this?

243
00:22:34,690 --> 00:22:38,730
You give me Neo, or we all die, 
right here, right now.

244
00:22:39,690 --> 00:22:42,610
Interesting deal.

245
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:49,620
You are really ready to die 
for this man?

246
00:22:50,740 --> 00:22:53,330
- Believe it. 
- She'll do it.

247
00:22:53,910 --> 00:22:56,750
If she has to, 
she'll kill every one of us.

248
00:22:56,920 --> 00:22:58,380
She's in love.

249
00:22:59,290 --> 00:23:04,630
It is remarkable how similar the pattern 
of love is to the pattern of insanity.

250
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:06,380
Time's up.

251
00:23:06,590 --> 00:23:08,090
What's it gonna be, Merv?

252
00:23:12,770 --> 00:23:16,600
Okay. You got yourself in here...

253
00:23:16,810 --> 00:23:19,360
...you can get yourself out.

254
00:24:07,030 --> 00:24:08,360
Are you ready for us?

255
00:24:08,530 --> 00:24:11,530
Almost, sir. They got 
some pretty ancient hacks here.

256
00:24:11,700 --> 00:24:13,870
- But you found Neo? 
- Can't you see him?

257
00:24:13,990 --> 00:24:16,910
No, sir. We were reading something, 
but I couldn't tell what.

258
00:24:21,540 --> 00:24:23,040
I can't leave yet.

259
00:24:26,050 --> 00:24:28,380
I have to see her.

260
00:24:29,050 --> 00:24:31,260
Now?

261
00:24:32,390 --> 00:24:33,760
It's my last chance.

262
00:24:36,390 --> 00:24:38,730
That's it. That's the secret.

263
00:24:38,890 --> 00:24:41,060
- You've got to use your hands. 
- Why?

264
00:24:41,560 --> 00:24:44,230
Cookies need love like everything does.

265
00:24:46,030 --> 00:24:47,440
Neo!

266
00:24:47,860 --> 00:24:52,740
I was hoping to have these done 
before you got here. Oh, well.

267
00:24:53,820 --> 00:24:56,870
Sati, honey, I think it's time 
for a tasting.

268
00:24:57,160 --> 00:25:00,040
Take the bowl to Seraph 
and find out if they're ready.

269
00:25:00,210 --> 00:25:02,290
Okay.

270
00:25:02,920 --> 00:25:05,420
- I'm glad you got out. 
- Me too.

271
00:25:09,340 --> 00:25:12,680
So do you recognize me?

272
00:25:12,890 --> 00:25:16,100
- A part of you. 
- Yeah, that's how it works.

273
00:25:16,260 --> 00:25:19,100
Some bits you lose, 
some bits you keep.

274
00:25:19,270 --> 00:25:23,100
I don't yet recognize my face 
in the mirror...

275
00:25:24,690 --> 00:25:26,610
...but I still love candy.

276
00:25:29,110 --> 00:25:30,400
No, thank you.

277
00:25:30,610 --> 00:25:33,780
Remember what you were like 
when you first walked through my door?

278
00:25:33,950 --> 00:25:38,990
Jittery as a June bug. 
And now, just look at you.

279
00:25:39,200 --> 00:25:42,460
You sure did surprise me, Neo, 
and you still do.

280
00:25:42,870 --> 00:25:45,920
You gave me a few surprises too.

281
00:25:46,090 --> 00:25:48,340
I hope I helped.

282
00:25:48,550 --> 00:25:51,970
You helped me to get here, 
but my question is, why?

283
00:25:52,220 --> 00:25:53,930
Where is this going?

284
00:25:54,090 --> 00:25:56,640
- Where does it end? 
- I don't know.

285
00:25:56,930 --> 00:26:00,310
- You don't know or you won't tell me? 
- I told you before...

286
00:26:00,810 --> 00:26:05,810
...no one can see beyond a choice they 
don't understand, and I mean no one.

287
00:26:06,440 --> 00:26:10,320
- What choice? 
- It doesn't matter. It's my choice.

288
00:26:10,440 --> 00:26:12,990
I have mine to make, 
same as you have yours.

289
00:26:13,280 --> 00:26:16,160
Does that include what things 
to tell me and what not to?

290
00:26:16,320 --> 00:26:17,530
Of course not.

291
00:26:17,740 --> 00:26:19,950
Then why didn't you tell me 
about the Architect?

292
00:26:20,120 --> 00:26:24,330
About Zion and the ones before me? 
Why didn't you tell me the truth?

293
00:26:25,290 --> 00:26:29,170
- Because it wasn't time for you to know. 
- Who decided it wasn't time?

294
00:26:29,630 --> 00:26:32,210
You know who.

295
00:26:38,970 --> 00:26:41,180
I did.

296
00:26:41,680 --> 00:26:45,020
Then I think it's time for me to know 
a few more things.

297
00:26:45,140 --> 00:26:46,900
So do I.

298
00:26:47,270 --> 00:26:50,980
Tell me how I separated my mind 
from my body without jacking in.

299
00:26:51,190 --> 00:26:53,900
Tell me how I stopped four sentinels 
by thinking it.

300
00:26:54,530 --> 00:26:58,200
Tell me just what the hell 
is happening to me.

301
00:27:00,330 --> 00:27:03,870
The power of the One 
extends beyond this world.

302
00:27:04,040 --> 00:27:07,540
It reaches from here all the way back 
to where it came from.

303
00:27:07,710 --> 00:27:09,960
- Where? 
- The source.

304
00:27:10,170 --> 00:27:14,840
That's what you felt when you touched 
those sentinels, but you weren't ready.

305
00:27:15,340 --> 00:27:20,930
You should be dead, but apparently 
you weren't ready for that either.

306
00:27:22,890 --> 00:27:25,730
The Architect told me that 
if I didn't return to the source...

307
00:27:25,890 --> 00:27:27,730
...Zion would be destroyed tonight.

308
00:27:27,850 --> 00:27:32,230
Please. You and I may not be able 
to see beyond our own choices...

309
00:27:32,400 --> 00:27:35,110
...but that man can't see 
past any choice.

310
00:27:35,650 --> 00:27:39,410
- Why not? 
- He doesn't understand them. He can't.

311
00:27:39,570 --> 00:27:42,240
To him, they are variables 
in an equation.

312
00:27:42,410 --> 00:27:46,410
One at a time, each variable 
must be solved, then countered.

313
00:27:46,580 --> 00:27:50,290
That's his purpose. 
To balance the equation.

314
00:27:50,750 --> 00:27:52,840
What's your purpose?

315
00:27:53,050 --> 00:27:55,090
To unbalance it.

316
00:27:55,210 --> 00:27:57,300
Why? What do you want?

317
00:27:57,880 --> 00:28:01,430
I want the same thing you want, Neo.

318
00:28:01,550 --> 00:28:04,470
And I'm willing to go 
as far as you are to get it.

319
00:28:05,020 --> 00:28:07,480
The end of the war.

320
00:28:08,100 --> 00:28:09,560
Is it going to end?

321
00:28:10,350 --> 00:28:12,440
One way or another.

322
00:28:13,020 --> 00:28:16,360
Can Zion be saved?

323
00:28:16,780 --> 00:28:21,570
I'm sorry, I don't have the answer 
to that question, but...

324
00:28:22,450 --> 00:28:27,290
If there is an answer, there's only 
one place you're going to find it.

325
00:28:27,540 --> 00:28:30,170
- Where? 
- You know where.

326
00:28:32,130 --> 00:28:35,250
And if you can't find the answer...

327
00:28:35,460 --> 00:28:38,970
...then I'm afraid there may be 
no tomorrow for any of us.

328
00:28:40,590 --> 00:28:43,300
What does that mean?

329
00:28:47,310 --> 00:28:50,940
Everything that has a beginning...

330
00:28:51,100 --> 00:28:53,520
...has an end.

331
00:28:53,730 --> 00:28:56,650
I see the end coming.

332
00:28:56,820 --> 00:28:59,700
I see the darkness spreading.

333
00:28:59,900 --> 00:29:01,320
I see death.

334
00:29:02,070 --> 00:29:05,620
And you are all that stands in his way.

335
00:29:05,780 --> 00:29:07,120
Smith.

336
00:29:08,080 --> 00:29:12,370
Very soon, he is going to have the power 
to destroy this world.

337
00:29:12,580 --> 00:29:15,290
But I believe he won't stop there. 
He can't.

338
00:29:15,500 --> 00:29:18,550
He won't stop until 
there's nothing left at all.

339
00:29:18,840 --> 00:29:20,220
What is he?

340
00:29:20,420 --> 00:29:22,340
He is you.

341
00:29:22,510 --> 00:29:24,970
Your opposite, your negative.

342
00:29:25,140 --> 00:29:28,680
The result of the equation 
trying to balance itself out.

343
00:29:29,020 --> 00:29:32,900
- And if I can't stop him? 
- One way or another, Neo...

344
00:29:33,690 --> 00:29:36,980
...this war is going to end.

345
00:29:37,150 --> 00:29:42,030
Tonight, the future of both worlds 
will be in your hands...

346
00:29:42,200 --> 00:29:43,990
...or in his.

347
00:30:00,510 --> 00:30:03,090
How are you feeling? 
Are you all right?

348
00:30:10,220 --> 00:30:12,560
I need time.

349
00:30:17,230 --> 00:30:20,780
- That figures. 
- Captain Roland.

350
00:30:20,980 --> 00:30:23,280
- What's up, Maggie? 
- Bane is. He's conscious.

351
00:30:23,490 --> 00:30:25,610
Good. Maybe he's got some answers.

352
00:30:30,700 --> 00:30:32,580
Mm!

353
00:30:32,750 --> 00:30:35,620
I love that smell.

354
00:30:36,710 --> 00:30:39,750
I sure am going to miss it.

355
00:30:40,420 --> 00:30:43,420
- Oracle. 
- I know.

356
00:30:43,670 --> 00:30:44,930
I know.

357
00:30:45,180 --> 00:30:47,800
Sati, honey.

358
00:30:48,930 --> 00:30:51,220
Take a few cookies and go with Seraph.

359
00:30:51,430 --> 00:30:54,230
Can I come back? 
I would like to come back.

360
00:30:54,390 --> 00:30:57,770
- I would like that too. 
- Then I'll see you tomorrow.

361
00:31:00,190 --> 00:31:02,940
I hope so, hon, I hope so.

362
00:31:25,470 --> 00:31:26,970
I'm scared, Seraph.

363
00:31:28,590 --> 00:31:30,470
Come.

364
00:32:13,600 --> 00:32:16,350
He's following us.

365
00:32:20,520 --> 00:32:24,360
Well, well, it's been a long time.

366
00:32:25,860 --> 00:32:28,860
I remember chasing you 
was like chasing a ghost.

367
00:32:29,280 --> 00:32:31,030
I have beaten you before.

368
00:32:31,530 --> 00:32:36,120
Yes, true, but as you can see, 
things are a little different now.

369
00:32:37,870 --> 00:32:40,870
And you must be the last exile.

370
00:32:41,540 --> 00:32:45,050
- The Oracle told me about you. 
- Really?

371
00:32:45,300 --> 00:32:47,130
What did she say about me?

372
00:32:47,550 --> 00:32:49,260
That you were a bad man.

373
00:32:49,550 --> 00:32:54,260
Oh, I'm not so bad, 
once you get to know me.

374
00:33:22,920 --> 00:33:27,460
The great and powerful Oracle, 
we meet at last.

375
00:33:30,380 --> 00:33:34,760
I suppose you've been 
expecting me, right?

376
00:33:34,930 --> 00:33:37,310
The all-knowing Oracle 
is never surprised.

377
00:33:37,510 --> 00:33:40,640
How can she be? She knows everything.

378
00:33:41,390 --> 00:33:45,560
But if that's true, then why is she here 
if she knew I was coming?

379
00:33:45,730 --> 00:33:47,730
Why wouldn't she leave?

380
00:33:53,280 --> 00:33:55,780
Maybe you knew I would do that, 
maybe you didn't.

381
00:33:55,950 --> 00:33:59,490
If you did, that means you baked those 
cookies and set that plate there...

382
00:33:59,700 --> 00:34:01,410
...deliberately, purposefully...

383
00:34:01,580 --> 00:34:05,580
...which means that you're sitting there 
also deliberately, purposefully.

384
00:34:06,630 --> 00:34:08,460
What did you do with Sati?

385
00:34:09,210 --> 00:34:13,800
"Cookies need love 
like everything does."

386
00:34:15,800 --> 00:34:17,260
You are a bastard.

387
00:34:18,100 --> 00:34:20,470
You would know, Mom.

388
00:34:24,600 --> 00:34:26,650
Do what you're here to do.

389
00:34:27,150 --> 00:34:29,150
Yes, ma'am.

390
00:35:13,820 --> 00:35:18,320
I really wish I could help, but I just... 
I don't remember any of it.

391
00:35:20,030 --> 00:35:23,910
What about the cuts on your arms? 
Those cuts are more than one day old.

392
00:35:24,540 --> 00:35:27,120
Yeah, definitely.

393
00:35:27,330 --> 00:35:29,580
You're right about that, sir.

394
00:35:30,130 --> 00:35:33,420
They look like they 
might be self-inflicted.

395
00:35:33,630 --> 00:35:37,840
But why would I do something 
like that to myself?

396
00:35:38,050 --> 00:35:42,890
Unless, of course, I wasn't myself.

397
00:35:43,060 --> 00:35:47,730
But if I'm not me, then who am I?

398
00:35:52,480 --> 00:35:56,570
- Has this man been tested for VDTs? 
- Yes, sir. It was negative.

399
00:35:57,320 --> 00:36:00,450
But he is showing a lot 
of unusual neural activity.

400
00:36:00,660 --> 00:36:03,950
Some cross-synaptic firing, 
as well as signs of recent trauma...

401
00:36:04,160 --> 00:36:07,960
...with fresh fibrotic scarring 
throughout the cortex.

402
00:36:08,330 --> 00:36:12,960
I want the truth. I don't care 
what it takes. Make him remember.

403
00:36:34,440 --> 00:36:35,730
Sir, we found her.

404
00:36:35,940 --> 00:36:37,280
- The <i>Logos</i>? 
- Yes, sir.

405
00:36:37,400 --> 00:36:39,490
About time we had 
some goddamn good news.

406
00:37:09,640 --> 00:37:12,650
Are the thermals picking up 
any signs of life?

407
00:37:13,650 --> 00:37:15,270
No, sir. Nothing yet.

408
00:37:15,480 --> 00:37:19,110
- What about the ship? 
- Holographic says the hull's intact.

409
00:37:19,280 --> 00:37:22,320
- Drop down and keep a man in the turret. 
- Yes, sir.

410
00:37:32,670 --> 00:37:36,540
Get a full diagnostic on that ship 
as fast as humanly possible.

411
00:37:54,310 --> 00:37:55,690
Careful, sir.

412
00:37:56,110 --> 00:38:00,360
The squids are sneaky bastards. 
It could be a trap.

413
00:38:25,890 --> 00:38:27,890
What was that?

414
00:38:29,890 --> 00:38:33,060
You can put that shit away, 
boys. All she needs is a jump.

415
00:38:34,730 --> 00:38:37,730
- Niobe. 
- Morpheus.

416
00:38:41,690 --> 00:38:44,070
- Are you all right? 
- Yes, I'm fine.

417
00:38:44,240 --> 00:38:47,070
We didn't know what happened after...

418
00:38:48,910 --> 00:38:52,040
- I'm sorry. 
- It's okay.

419
00:38:52,200 --> 00:38:54,250
I'm happy to see you too.

420
00:38:55,080 --> 00:38:56,960
- Did you get Neo out? 
- Yes.

421
00:38:57,170 --> 00:38:59,290
- How did you know about that? 
- The Oracle.

422
00:38:59,500 --> 00:39:02,090
- You saw her? 
- Just before the sentinels found us.

423
00:39:02,590 --> 00:39:06,760
- What did she tell you? 
- The same thing she always does.

424
00:39:07,930 --> 00:39:10,760
Exactly what I needed to hear.

425
00:39:12,390 --> 00:39:15,270
In 12 hours, the machines 
will breach the dock walls.

426
00:39:15,600 --> 00:39:19,940
Every simulation we've run, we've seen 
that once the machines are inside...

427
00:39:20,110 --> 00:39:22,780
...the odds of our survival 
decrease dramatically.

428
00:39:22,940 --> 00:39:24,900
Thus, our primary objective must be...

429
00:39:25,110 --> 00:39:28,570
...to destroy or disable the diggers 
inside the dock.

430
00:39:28,740 --> 00:39:32,950
If we can do that, perhaps we can 
prevent them from reaching the city.

431
00:39:33,120 --> 00:39:36,290
If not, the only place we will be able 
to mount a defense...

432
00:39:36,460 --> 00:39:38,580
...will be at the entrance of the temple.

433
00:39:38,790 --> 00:39:41,500
It is small and will force 
them into a bottleneck...

434
00:39:41,710 --> 00:39:44,800
...allowing us to concentrate 
the remainder of our defense.

435
00:39:45,130 --> 00:39:48,130
We understand that you've requested 
additional volunteers.

436
00:39:48,300 --> 00:39:50,800
- That is correct. 
- Precisely what size force...

437
00:39:50,970 --> 00:39:54,220
...are you planning to commit 
to the primary dock objective?

438
00:39:54,430 --> 00:39:57,980
Right now, the entire APU Corps 
and half the infantry.

439
00:39:58,100 --> 00:40:01,150
- Half the infantry? 
- If it were up to me, councillor...

440
00:40:01,270 --> 00:40:04,610
...I'd take every man, woman and child, 
put a gun in their hand...

441
00:40:04,780 --> 00:40:06,650
...and march them into that dock.

442
00:40:06,820 --> 00:40:09,530
Perhaps it is best 
that it is not up to you.

443
00:40:09,740 --> 00:40:11,700
Time will tell, councillor.

444
00:40:11,990 --> 00:40:14,660
Commander, just one more question.

445
00:40:14,830 --> 00:40:17,120
Has there been word 
from the <i>Nebuchadnezzar</i>?

446
00:40:17,290 --> 00:40:20,710
None, and at this point there's no reason 
to expect there will be.

447
00:40:20,920 --> 00:40:22,880
Perhaps.

448
00:40:23,090 --> 00:40:24,460
But we can hope.

449
00:40:24,840 --> 00:40:28,050
I'm afraid hope is an indulgence 
I don't have time for.

450
00:40:39,390 --> 00:40:42,270
What the shit is going on over here?

451
00:40:42,440 --> 00:40:45,940
An accident, sir. I didn't see...

452
00:40:46,110 --> 00:40:48,280
- I'm sorry. 
- Who the hell are you?

453
00:40:48,450 --> 00:40:50,740
A unit volunteer, sir.

454
00:40:51,360 --> 00:40:55,120
What's a pod-born pencil-neck like you 
doing volunteering for my Corps?

455
00:40:55,790 --> 00:40:59,290
I want to do my part, sir. 
We gotta hold the dock.

456
00:41:00,620 --> 00:41:02,710
- How old are you, kid? 
- Eighteen.

457
00:41:02,920 --> 00:41:06,000
Should have said 16, 
I might have believed that.

458
00:41:06,300 --> 00:41:07,590
Okay, I'm 16.

459
00:41:07,800 --> 00:41:11,340
Minimum age for the Corps is 18. 
Sixteen's too young.

460
00:41:11,550 --> 00:41:16,350
The machines don't care how old I am. 
They'll kill me just the same.

461
00:41:16,970 --> 00:41:18,850
Ain't that the goddamn truth.

462
00:41:19,390 --> 00:41:22,650
Give me a chance, sir. 
I won't let you down.

463
00:41:23,400 --> 00:41:24,730
You do...

464
00:41:24,980 --> 00:41:28,530
...and you'll find me and the machines 
have got something in common.

465
00:41:41,500 --> 00:41:44,170
Okay, charge the igniter.

466
00:41:50,300 --> 00:41:52,180
She lives again.

467
00:41:52,510 --> 00:41:55,680
Want us to patch an uplink to reload 
the operations software, Sparky?

468
00:41:55,850 --> 00:41:59,180
That'd be swell. Could you clean 
the windshield while you're at it?

469
00:42:03,980 --> 00:42:06,560
Uplinks in place. 
I'm bringing her back online.

470
00:42:06,770 --> 00:42:09,530
Looking good, except, uh...

471
00:42:11,320 --> 00:42:13,360
Something's wrong 
with the Matrix feed.

472
00:42:13,530 --> 00:42:16,740
No, there's not. You're looking 
at what we're looking at.

473
00:42:16,950 --> 00:42:20,410
<i>- What's going on in there?</i> 
- Whatever it is, it can't be good.

474
00:42:21,450 --> 00:42:23,410
The machines have taken Junction 21.

475
00:42:24,370 --> 00:42:27,460
The way I see it, if we drop down 
from broadcast here...

476
00:42:27,670 --> 00:42:30,260
...intersect 153, we might surprise them.

477
00:42:30,840 --> 00:42:35,050
We'll go first, hammer as deep 
as we can, then blow our EMP.

478
00:42:35,220 --> 00:42:39,220
Hopefully we can punch a hole 
big enough for you to get through.

479
00:42:40,720 --> 00:42:45,560
It ain't pretty, but the way I see it, 
it's the only way back.

480
00:42:45,730 --> 00:42:47,190
No, it's not.

481
00:42:47,400 --> 00:42:50,440
There's another way. A support line.

482
00:42:50,650 --> 00:42:54,400
It drops down right here, 
1000 meters short of 21.

483
00:42:54,700 --> 00:42:58,580
If we're lucky, we may be able to 
slip down without them ever knowing.

484
00:42:58,740 --> 00:43:01,200
That's a mechanical line. 
It's impossible.

485
00:43:01,370 --> 00:43:03,410
- No one can pilot mechanical. 
- I can.

486
00:43:03,540 --> 00:43:05,580
- Bullshit. 
- I've done it.

487
00:43:05,750 --> 00:43:08,960
- That was a long time ago, Niobe. 
- I said I can do it.

488
00:43:09,170 --> 00:43:13,760
So what? You'll be the only one that can. 
There's no way we can follow you.

489
00:43:16,260 --> 00:43:17,840
Hi.

490
00:43:19,510 --> 00:43:24,060
I know time is always against us. 
I'm sorry that I took so long.

491
00:43:24,270 --> 00:43:28,060
- But I wanted to be sure. 
- Sure of what?

492
00:43:28,230 --> 00:43:30,320
- I know what I have to do. 
- What?

493
00:43:30,520 --> 00:43:33,780
There's no easy way to say this, 
so I'll just say it.

494
00:43:33,940 --> 00:43:36,610
- I have to take one of the ships. 
- What?

495
00:43:36,740 --> 00:43:38,490
To go where?

496
00:43:39,450 --> 00:43:40,780
To the machine city.

497
00:43:45,540 --> 00:43:47,620
I know it's difficult to understand.

498
00:43:47,750 --> 00:43:50,290
No, it's not. You're out 
of your goddamn mind.

499
00:43:50,630 --> 00:43:51,960
I still have to go.

500
00:43:52,130 --> 00:43:55,300
In 100 years, no ship has been 
within 100 kilometers of it.

501
00:43:55,550 --> 00:43:58,180
- You'll never make it. 
- I have to try.

502
00:43:58,380 --> 00:44:01,350
- Is this what the Oracle has told you? 
- No.

503
00:44:02,060 --> 00:44:04,850
This is asinine. If you want 
to kill yourself, do it...

504
00:44:05,060 --> 00:44:07,140
...but do it without 
wasting our ships.

505
00:44:07,270 --> 00:44:10,270
- You have to believe me. I have to go. 
- Bullshit!

506
00:44:10,440 --> 00:44:13,610
I am the captain of this ship. 
I say where it has to go!

507
00:44:13,820 --> 00:44:17,650
And this ship will go to hell 
long before I let you take it anywhere.

508
00:44:21,320 --> 00:44:25,330
- He can take mine. 
- You can't do that.

509
00:44:26,330 --> 00:44:29,290
Don't try to tell me 
what I can or cannot do...

510
00:44:29,460 --> 00:44:31,710
...with my ship 
after that little speech.

511
00:44:31,920 --> 00:44:36,340
- But for chrissake, Niobe... 
- I'll pilot this ship, he can take mine.

512
00:44:36,840 --> 00:44:40,470
If we leave inside the hour, 
we'll reach Zion as the machines do.

513
00:44:40,680 --> 00:44:43,180
That's as good a plan as any.

514
00:44:43,350 --> 00:44:47,100
It's a waste. A goddamn waste.

515
00:44:52,690 --> 00:44:55,860
Two ships, two directions.

516
00:44:56,030 --> 00:44:59,200
Sounds like providence, 
doesn't it, Morpheus?

517
00:44:59,860 --> 00:45:03,030
- You've never believed in the One. 
- I still don't.

518
00:45:03,200 --> 00:45:04,870
Then why are you doing this?

519
00:45:06,490 --> 00:45:08,080
I believe in him.

520
00:45:09,870 --> 00:45:11,920
Thank you.

521
00:45:16,840 --> 00:45:19,880
- What's that for? 
- To help you relax.

522
00:45:20,010 --> 00:45:22,890
To make it easier for you to remember.

523
00:45:23,550 --> 00:45:25,720
What if I don't want to remember?

524
00:45:26,720 --> 00:45:28,770
Why would you want that?

525
00:45:28,980 --> 00:45:32,060
What if I blew that EMP?

526
00:45:33,150 --> 00:45:35,060
What if I did destroy those ships....

527
00:45:35,230 --> 00:45:40,030
...and I am responsible 
for the deaths of all those men?

528
00:45:42,070 --> 00:45:45,070
If I did that...

529
00:45:45,240 --> 00:45:48,950
...it wouldn't be very safe 
for me here, would it?

530
00:45:58,840 --> 00:46:03,090
Of course, it might not be 
very safe for you either.

531
00:46:10,930 --> 00:46:13,100
I'm ready.

532
00:46:14,190 --> 00:46:16,150
Trinity...

533
00:46:17,110 --> 00:46:19,780
...there's something I have to say.

534
00:46:22,860 --> 00:46:25,660
Something you need to understand.

535
00:46:26,870 --> 00:46:29,740
I know I'm supposed to go.

536
00:46:29,910 --> 00:46:32,160
But beyond that...

537
00:46:33,210 --> 00:46:35,630
...I don't know. I...

538
00:46:35,790 --> 00:46:39,670
I know. You don't think 
you're coming back.

539
00:46:41,460 --> 00:46:46,300
I knew it the moment you said you had 
to leave. I could see it in your face.

540
00:46:46,470 --> 00:46:49,140
Just like you knew the moment 
you looked at me...

541
00:46:49,310 --> 00:46:51,680
...that I was coming with you.

542
00:46:53,810 --> 00:46:55,520
I'm scared, Trin.

543
00:46:55,900 --> 00:46:57,810
So am I.

544
00:46:58,650 --> 00:47:02,320
It took me 10 minutes 
to buckle up one boot.

545
00:47:03,320 --> 00:47:05,360
But I'll tell you something.

546
00:47:05,570 --> 00:47:08,450
Six hours ago, I told the Merovingian...

547
00:47:08,660 --> 00:47:11,620
...I was ready to give anything 
and everything for you.

548
00:47:14,160 --> 00:47:16,750
Do you know what's changed 
in the last six hours?

549
00:47:16,960 --> 00:47:18,460
No.

550
00:47:19,000 --> 00:47:20,340
Nothing.

551
00:47:33,770 --> 00:47:36,020
<i>- Finished loading ammunition?</i> 
- Just about.

552
00:47:36,270 --> 00:47:38,520
Let's move it. We are out of time.

553
00:47:38,770 --> 00:47:41,020
You're not leaving them anything?

554
00:47:41,150 --> 00:47:43,360
He said he didn't need it.

555
00:47:47,280 --> 00:47:50,660
I ain't saying goodbye. 
I'm saying good luck.

556
00:47:51,120 --> 00:47:52,910
Thank you.

557
00:47:57,790 --> 00:48:00,670
I can only hope you know 
what you're doing.

558
00:48:00,880 --> 00:48:02,250
Me too.

559
00:48:06,510 --> 00:48:08,010
It was an honor, sir.

560
00:48:12,310 --> 00:48:14,350
No, the honor is still mine.

561
00:48:28,240 --> 00:48:31,280
<i>- We're ready, sir.</i> 
- About damn time.

562
00:48:32,530 --> 00:48:36,080
We're already late, captain, 
so let's hit it and hit it hard.

563
00:48:39,830 --> 00:48:41,710
Bye, baby.

564
00:48:41,920 --> 00:48:43,750
Take good care of them.

565
00:49:05,570 --> 00:49:07,320
Ready?

566
00:49:15,120 --> 00:49:17,120
Engine's still firing.

567
00:49:17,370 --> 00:49:19,960
Must be a fuse. I'll check it out.

568
00:49:49,650 --> 00:49:52,740
Neo, it's Bane. He's psychotic!

569
00:49:53,570 --> 00:49:56,120
You're gonna pay for that.

570
00:49:57,330 --> 00:50:00,250
- Twenty-seven kilometers to go. 
<i>- We got an emergency.</i>

571
00:50:00,410 --> 00:50:02,920
- What is it, AK? 
<i>- It's Maggie, sir.</i>

572
00:50:03,080 --> 00:50:05,250
<i>She's dead, murdered. 
I think it was Bane.</i>

573
00:50:05,420 --> 00:50:07,920
Goddamn it.

574
00:50:09,880 --> 00:50:13,260
I knew it. I knew he was 
out of his goddamn mind.

575
00:50:13,430 --> 00:50:15,260
He fired that EMP.

576
00:50:15,430 --> 00:50:19,100
Goddamn it, I should have 
beaten it out of him.

577
00:50:19,270 --> 00:50:22,140
We searched the whole ship, captain. 
He ain't here.

578
00:50:23,850 --> 00:50:26,150
- I know where he is. 
- The <i>Logos.</i>

579
00:50:27,860 --> 00:50:29,610
- We gotta go back. 
- Too late.

580
00:50:29,780 --> 00:50:32,650
- What if they need our help? 
- It's too dangerous.

581
00:50:32,860 --> 00:50:34,740
- Why? 
- Because if he's killed them...

582
00:50:34,950 --> 00:50:36,490
...he'll control another EMP.

583
00:50:38,030 --> 00:50:41,830
At this point, they're on their own. 
Just like us.

584
00:50:43,460 --> 00:50:45,120
Mr. Anderson.

585
00:50:45,960 --> 00:50:49,960
I see you are as predictable in this world 
as you are in the other.

586
00:50:50,420 --> 00:50:51,960
- What? 
- He's out of his mind.

587
00:50:52,130 --> 00:50:55,090
It might appear that way. 
But Mr. Anderson and I know...

588
00:50:55,260 --> 00:50:58,140
...that appearances can be deceiving.

589
00:50:58,300 --> 00:51:02,140
Confused, Mr. Anderson? 
It'll all become clear in a moment.

590
00:51:02,310 --> 00:51:05,520
Thank you for bringing me the gun. 
You can set it down there.

591
00:51:05,730 --> 00:51:07,810
Don't do it.

592
00:51:07,940 --> 00:51:12,150
- Shoot. Shoot now. 
- Yes, shoot. Fry us. Burn us alive.

593
00:51:12,400 --> 00:51:15,650
Do it. If you don't, he'll kill us both.

594
00:51:16,740 --> 00:51:20,830
Look at him. He knows 
he should do it, but he won't.

595
00:51:20,990 --> 00:51:23,080
- He can't. 
- Do it.

596
00:51:31,590 --> 00:51:35,010
Back away from the gun 
and turn around.

597
00:51:42,010 --> 00:51:43,310
Let her go.

598
00:51:56,530 --> 00:51:59,530
Somehow familiar, isn't it?

599
00:51:59,700 --> 00:52:03,870
We've been here before, 
you and I, remember?

600
00:52:04,040 --> 00:52:07,710
I do. I think of nothing else.

601
00:52:12,290 --> 00:52:15,630
- What do you want? 
- I want what you want.

602
00:52:18,720 --> 00:52:23,100
Yes. That's it, Mr. Anderson.

603
00:52:23,260 --> 00:52:25,180
Look past the flesh.

604
00:52:25,390 --> 00:52:30,730
Look through the soft gelatin of these 
dull cow eyes and see your enemy.

605
00:52:32,770 --> 00:52:35,820
- No. 
- Oh, yes, Mr. Anderson.

606
00:52:36,150 --> 00:52:39,110
- It can't be. 
- There's nowhere I can't go.

607
00:52:39,280 --> 00:52:42,160
There is nowhere I won't find you.

608
00:52:42,320 --> 00:52:46,370
- It's impossible. 
- Not impossible.

609
00:52:46,950 --> 00:52:48,500
Inevitable.

610
00:52:50,330 --> 00:52:52,330
Goodbye, Mr. Anderson.

611
00:52:52,500 --> 00:52:54,170
This is it. It's gotta be.

612
00:53:39,840 --> 00:53:40,880
Oh, no.

613
00:53:59,070 --> 00:54:02,950
I wish you could see yourself, 
Mr. Anderson.

614
00:54:07,410 --> 00:54:09,620
Blind messiah.

615
00:54:13,870 --> 00:54:17,250
You're a symbol for all of your kind, 
Mr. Anderson.

616
00:54:20,090 --> 00:54:22,260
Helpless.

617
00:54:24,590 --> 00:54:26,760
Pathetic.

618
00:54:29,680 --> 00:54:33,980
Just waiting to be put out 
of your misery.

619
00:54:39,280 --> 00:54:40,730
I can see you.

620
00:54:49,620 --> 00:54:52,450
It's not over, Mr. Anderson.

621
00:54:52,620 --> 00:54:54,500
It's not over.

622
00:55:07,930 --> 00:55:11,310
- Trinity! 
- Neo.

623
00:55:12,890 --> 00:55:14,310
Neo.

624
00:55:17,310 --> 00:55:20,480
Oh, no. Your eyes.

625
00:55:20,650 --> 00:55:22,820
I'll be okay.

626
00:55:24,150 --> 00:55:26,320
It's all right, Trin.

627
00:55:28,070 --> 00:55:30,990
But I think you're gonna have to drive.

628
00:55:37,580 --> 00:55:40,670
Seismic's projecting 
22 minutes to breach.

629
00:55:40,840 --> 00:55:44,510
They can't know we don't have an EMP. 
They'll have to attack in waves.

630
00:55:44,670 --> 00:55:49,340
Concentrate our offense on the diggers. 
Order the APUs into position.

631
00:55:49,600 --> 00:55:51,060
Yes, sir.

632
00:56:20,880 --> 00:56:23,590
Come on, move.

633
00:56:55,740 --> 00:56:57,410
All right!

634
00:56:57,580 --> 00:56:59,410
This is it.

635
00:56:59,580 --> 00:57:04,630
Now, you all know me, 
so I'll just say this as simple as I can.

636
00:57:05,420 --> 00:57:09,260
If it's our time to die, it's our time.

637
00:57:09,430 --> 00:57:14,930
All I ask is, if we have 
to give these bastards our lives...

638
00:57:15,100 --> 00:57:17,930
...we give them hell before we do!

639
00:57:18,180 --> 00:57:20,100
- Yeah! 
- Yeah!

640
00:57:34,910 --> 00:57:37,740
- You scared, Charra? 
- Shit, yeah.

641
00:57:38,790 --> 00:57:40,330
But I'll make you a deal.

642
00:57:41,040 --> 00:57:44,080
You keep loading, I keep shooting.

643
00:57:46,300 --> 00:57:48,170
Deal.

644
00:57:57,640 --> 00:58:00,640
- Holy Christ, would you look at that. 
- Quiet.

645
00:58:01,100 --> 00:58:03,980
- How far to the opening? 
- 1.4 kilometers.

646
00:58:04,230 --> 00:58:08,860
- We're still generating too hot a field. 
- Ghost, kill all auxiliary systems.

647
00:58:09,070 --> 00:58:12,820
- Full manual. Drop down four pads. 
- It'll bottom out.

648
00:58:22,830 --> 00:58:26,170
- Easy, baby. 
- Seven hundred meters.

649
00:58:28,670 --> 00:58:31,340
If we can just get close enough...

650
00:58:35,840 --> 00:58:37,220
Six hundred meters.

651
00:58:38,350 --> 00:58:39,970
There.

652
00:58:47,520 --> 00:58:49,190
Shit!

653
00:58:51,490 --> 00:58:53,900
- Jig's up, here they come. 
- Give me full power.

654
00:58:54,110 --> 00:58:56,410
Man the gun turrets, 
every goddamn one of them. Go!

655
00:59:13,840 --> 00:59:16,300
I'm coming, baby.

656
00:59:25,190 --> 00:59:27,190
Here they come.

657
00:59:31,480 --> 00:59:35,570
<i>- Slow down, this ain't the</i> Logos. 
- Hang on to your lunch, here we go.

658
00:59:44,290 --> 00:59:47,370
Holy Christ, I didn't know 
this ship could do that.

659
01:00:39,260 --> 01:00:40,760
Breach! The dock is breached!

660
01:01:01,780 --> 01:01:03,740
Knuckle up!

661
01:01:17,050 --> 01:01:18,670
For Zion!

662
01:03:26,840 --> 01:03:28,600
Shit.

663
01:03:33,390 --> 01:03:35,560
Come on, let's go.

664
01:03:41,270 --> 01:03:42,650
Knuckle up!

665
01:03:57,790 --> 01:03:59,130
Reload!

666
01:04:00,880 --> 01:04:02,800
Reload nine!

667
01:04:09,470 --> 01:04:10,760
Go, go! Move, move!

668
01:04:23,150 --> 01:04:24,820
Watch your left!

669
01:04:25,900 --> 01:04:28,150
Don't let them through!

670
01:04:31,160 --> 01:04:32,660
Zuka!

671
01:05:09,650 --> 01:05:11,410
Oh, my God.

672
01:05:24,960 --> 01:05:28,590
Where the hell's my infantry? I want 
that goddamn machine taken down!

673
01:06:02,580 --> 01:06:03,920
Dig this!

674
01:06:08,090 --> 01:06:09,380
Oh, shit!

675
01:06:29,110 --> 01:06:30,990
- Yeah! 
- Bogey two at the breach point!

676
01:06:31,190 --> 01:06:32,450
Goddamn it!

677
01:06:58,470 --> 01:07:00,640
Shit, she's got a fat ass.

678
01:07:09,940 --> 01:07:13,360
- Keep them off me! 
- Christ, there's a shitstorm of them.

679
01:07:45,270 --> 01:07:47,900
- Captain, you see that? 
- They're after the radio. Stop them!

680
01:07:55,700 --> 01:07:57,030
Damn it!

681
01:08:21,890 --> 01:08:23,350
Yeah.

682
01:08:35,070 --> 01:08:36,900
Grab my belt.

683
01:08:47,370 --> 01:08:48,790
Just give me one clean shot.

684
01:08:55,670 --> 01:08:57,380
Damn it!

685
01:09:19,570 --> 01:09:21,160
Charra!

686
01:09:26,120 --> 01:09:28,790
- I got incoming! 
- We got a dock full of incoming!

687
01:09:28,960 --> 01:09:31,460
- Yes, sir. But this is different, sir. 
- What?

688
01:09:32,130 --> 01:09:33,790
I think it's one of ours, sir.

689
01:09:33,960 --> 01:09:36,920
- That's impossible. 
- Holographics are trying to confirm.

690
01:09:37,130 --> 01:09:38,840
Contact them. 
I want access codes.

691
01:09:39,050 --> 01:09:41,590
We're trying, sir. 
There's no response.

692
01:09:42,930 --> 01:09:45,640
It's a trick. That's not one of ours, 
it can't be.

693
01:09:45,810 --> 01:09:49,600
That's a mechanical line. 
No one can pilot mechanical.

694
01:09:59,900 --> 01:10:03,160
- Forward aft, 30 degrees at 80 percent. 
- Thirty degrees, 80.

695
01:10:06,160 --> 01:10:09,200
- Lower starboard 60 degrees, 20 percent. 
- Sixty degrees.

696
01:10:12,080 --> 01:10:15,040
- Shit! Come on, keep up! 
- I'm trying!

697
01:10:35,020 --> 01:10:37,730
Sir, holographic confirms. 
It's the <i>Hammer</i>, sir.

698
01:10:38,270 --> 01:10:39,570
How can that be?

699
01:10:39,780 --> 01:10:41,740
It's under attack, sustaining damage.

700
01:10:41,950 --> 01:10:44,700
At present velocity, 
it'll reach Gate Three in 12 minutes.

701
01:10:44,860 --> 01:10:47,240
Their EMP could take out every sentinel.

702
01:10:48,120 --> 01:10:51,540
It'd take out more than that. 
It'll wipe out our defense system.

703
01:10:51,700 --> 01:10:53,920
We blow an EMP inside, 
we lose the dock.

704
01:10:54,540 --> 01:10:56,380
Sir, we already lost the dock.

705
01:11:00,550 --> 01:11:01,880
Open the gate.

706
01:11:03,720 --> 01:11:07,930
Gate Three is not responding! 
We've taken critical damage, sir!

707
01:11:08,140 --> 01:11:10,390
We've lost control! 
We can't open it!

708
01:11:20,150 --> 01:11:21,440
There's the exit.

709
01:11:21,650 --> 01:11:25,070
On my mark, give me full power 
90 degrees to lower-left starboard.

710
01:11:25,570 --> 01:11:27,370
Full power...

711
01:11:27,570 --> 01:11:28,910
...ninety degrees.

712
01:11:35,250 --> 01:11:36,540
Now!

713
01:11:44,050 --> 01:11:46,090
Hold on, baby.

714
01:11:50,720 --> 01:11:52,600
Goddamn, woman, you can drive.

715
01:11:52,770 --> 01:11:54,770
We ain't home yet. 
What about the gate?

716
01:11:57,400 --> 01:11:58,860
Sentinels are inside the dock.

717
01:12:00,230 --> 01:12:01,570
Are we too late?

718
01:12:31,140 --> 01:12:33,850
- How many APUs are operational? 
- Thirteen, sir.

719
01:12:34,060 --> 01:12:36,020
Get me the one closest to Gate Three.

720
01:13:04,420 --> 01:13:05,670
Reload!

721
01:13:05,920 --> 01:13:07,170
He's pissing metal.

722
01:13:10,680 --> 01:13:12,180
Go!

723
01:13:26,690 --> 01:13:28,030
Go!

724
01:13:49,970 --> 01:13:51,720
Heads up! They're coming around!

725
01:14:04,730 --> 01:14:06,270
Behind you!

726
01:14:19,830 --> 01:14:21,660
It's jammed!

727
01:14:27,420 --> 01:14:30,130
Forget it, kid! Get out of here!

728
01:14:31,260 --> 01:14:32,930
Got it!

729
01:15:01,410 --> 01:15:03,290
Captain Mifune.

730
01:15:06,420 --> 01:15:08,290
Oh, no.

731
01:15:08,790 --> 01:15:10,130
They're coming.

732
01:15:12,470 --> 01:15:14,090
They're coming.

733
01:15:15,380 --> 01:15:16,680
The <i>Hammer.</i>

734
01:15:17,260 --> 01:15:18,640
What?

735
01:15:19,060 --> 01:15:21,810
You have to open that gate.

736
01:15:22,600 --> 01:15:24,310
Cut the counterweights.

737
01:15:26,480 --> 01:15:27,770
You can do it.

738
01:15:28,650 --> 01:15:31,230
Hurry. There's no time.

739
01:15:53,670 --> 01:15:55,840
- Lock that down! 
- Kill the feeder!

740
01:15:56,260 --> 01:15:59,350
We won't make it. 
We gotta blow the EMP now.

741
01:15:59,510 --> 01:16:02,680
Come on, someone, please.

742
01:16:17,360 --> 01:16:19,240
Keep the weight forward.

743
01:16:21,280 --> 01:16:23,040
Light as a feather. 
Light as a feather.

744
01:16:27,370 --> 01:16:31,380
Holographic reports Captain Mifune's 
APU is up and moving to Gate Three.

745
01:16:37,380 --> 01:16:39,510
Don't over-squeeze the trigger.

746
01:16:50,190 --> 01:16:52,230
Mifune's APU just reached Gate Three.

747
01:16:52,400 --> 01:16:55,190
- How much time? 
- Two minutes to impact.

748
01:16:55,900 --> 01:16:59,700
- Captain Mifune, do you copy? 
- I think his radio is down, sir.

749
01:16:59,860 --> 01:17:01,280
Mifune...

750
01:17:01,490 --> 01:17:03,080
...this is Lock.

751
01:17:03,330 --> 01:17:06,200
I don't know if you can hear me, 
but if you can...

752
01:17:06,370 --> 01:17:08,710
<i>...the</i> Hammer<i>'s two minutes away.</i>

753
01:17:09,250 --> 01:17:13,420
<i>You've got two minutes, captain, 
to get that gate open.</i>

754
01:17:15,090 --> 01:17:16,460
Link.

755
01:17:17,010 --> 01:17:19,260
Get to the main deck! 
Charge the EMP!

756
01:17:55,880 --> 01:17:57,510
Do it, kid.

757
01:18:01,550 --> 01:18:04,430
Neo. I believe.

758
01:18:13,480 --> 01:18:15,520
- Yes! 
- Can we make it?

759
01:18:16,900 --> 01:18:18,980
We ain't come this far.

760
01:18:31,160 --> 01:18:33,370
Almost home, almost home.

761
01:18:52,850 --> 01:18:54,400
Burn it, Link!

762
01:19:18,540 --> 01:19:21,550
- You did it. 
- No.

763
01:19:21,880 --> 01:19:23,510
We did it.

764
01:19:24,550 --> 01:19:25,930
You're a hell of a pilot.

765
01:19:39,650 --> 01:19:40,980
Link!

766
01:19:41,650 --> 01:19:43,320
- Zee? Zee! 
- Link!

767
01:19:50,330 --> 01:19:53,120
I knew you'd come. I knew it.

768
01:19:53,830 --> 01:19:55,790
I made a promise.

769
01:20:13,890 --> 01:20:15,890
Three captains, one ship.

770
01:20:16,060 --> 01:20:20,060
I'll assume the other ships were lost 
under equally pointless circumstances.

771
01:20:20,230 --> 01:20:21,860
Good to see you too, Jason.

772
01:20:22,070 --> 01:20:24,400
The Council's waiting to hear 
your explanation.

773
01:20:24,570 --> 01:20:28,700
Forgive me for not attending, 
but I have to try to salvage this debacle.

774
01:20:29,490 --> 01:20:32,080
Did I miss something? 
I thought we saved the dock.

775
01:20:32,240 --> 01:20:34,080
That's the problem with you people.

776
01:20:34,250 --> 01:20:36,790
You can't think but five minutes 
in front of you.

777
01:20:37,080 --> 01:20:40,710
That EMP knocked out almost every 
piece of hardware and every APU.

778
01:20:40,880 --> 01:20:43,800
If I were the machines, 
I'd send every sentinel here now.

779
01:20:44,090 --> 01:20:47,760
Save the dock, captain? 
You handed it to them on a silver platter.

780
01:20:53,510 --> 01:20:55,470
Come on, get it cut.

781
01:20:57,100 --> 01:20:58,440
The bridge is clear.

782
01:21:01,020 --> 01:21:02,900
Do you hear that?

783
01:21:05,280 --> 01:21:06,780
Get that cable run!

784
01:21:07,030 --> 01:21:10,780
- I want the system back online! 
- It's the dock. They've got incoming.

785
01:21:12,120 --> 01:21:14,450
Order everyone to fall back.

786
01:21:14,620 --> 01:21:17,330
Seal the shaft. Now.

787
01:21:18,120 --> 01:21:19,750
Move it!

788
01:21:23,130 --> 01:21:24,800
Oh, my God.

789
01:21:32,930 --> 01:21:35,140
- All clear. 
- Do it.

790
01:21:35,310 --> 01:21:37,470
- Go! Come on! Run! 
- Go!

791
01:21:53,780 --> 01:21:55,330
Your move.

792
01:21:56,490 --> 01:21:58,160
So you gave them your ship?

793
01:21:58,660 --> 01:22:02,830
- That is correct, councillor, I did. 
- Knowing what he planned to do with it?

794
01:22:04,500 --> 01:22:06,340
The Oracle said nothing of this?

795
01:22:07,340 --> 01:22:11,840
She told me Neo would need my help, 
and I would choose to help him or not.

796
01:22:12,180 --> 01:22:16,640
But what hope can a single vessel have 
against their entire defense system?

797
01:22:16,850 --> 01:22:20,020
None. It's completely impossible. 
But he wouldn't listen.

798
01:22:20,180 --> 01:22:24,520
He wouldn't even take any ammunition. 
He was totally out of his goddamn mind.

799
01:22:24,690 --> 01:22:27,520
No, he wasn't.

800
01:22:29,320 --> 01:22:31,990
Neo is doing what he believes 
he must do.

801
01:22:33,360 --> 01:22:36,620
I don't know if what he's doing is right. 
I don't know...

802
01:22:36,830 --> 01:22:39,410
...if he'll reach the machine city.

803
01:22:39,620 --> 01:22:42,870
And if he does, I don't know 
what he can do to save us.

804
01:22:44,210 --> 01:22:48,880
But I do know that as long as there is 
a single breath in his body...

805
01:22:50,340 --> 01:22:52,380
...he will not give up.

806
01:22:53,720 --> 01:22:55,220
And neither can we.

807
01:23:01,680 --> 01:23:03,020
Temperature's dropping.

808
01:23:06,560 --> 01:23:07,900
Here we go.

809
01:23:47,440 --> 01:23:49,150
We're over the fields, aren't we?

810
01:23:50,610 --> 01:23:51,940
How do you know that?

811
01:23:52,690 --> 01:23:54,530
I can feel them.

812
01:24:03,290 --> 01:24:04,960
Over there.

813
01:24:05,750 --> 01:24:09,630
There's our path. Can you see it? 
Three lines.

814
01:24:09,790 --> 01:24:11,130
Power lines.

815
01:24:12,090 --> 01:24:13,840
Follow them.

816
01:24:30,810 --> 01:24:32,650
What are they doing?

817
01:24:32,820 --> 01:24:34,530
I don't know.

818
01:24:35,490 --> 01:24:37,320
Lieutenant?

819
01:24:52,500 --> 01:24:53,840
Goddamn it.

820
01:24:54,170 --> 01:24:55,510
What do we do now?

821
01:25:00,180 --> 01:25:02,260
It is now a matter of time.

822
01:25:03,010 --> 01:25:05,520
The machines will breach 
the walls of this city.

823
01:25:06,850 --> 01:25:11,360
I recommend that the Council join the 
non-military personnel inside the temple.

824
01:25:12,020 --> 01:25:13,360
How long do we have?

825
01:25:13,860 --> 01:25:16,530
Two hours. Maybe less.

826
01:25:18,320 --> 01:25:22,530
My men have fortified the entrance with 
enough artillery to make our last stand.

827
01:25:24,370 --> 01:25:26,870
Beyond that, there isn't anything more 
I can do.

828
01:25:27,370 --> 01:25:30,870
Commander, do you think that 
we have any chance of surviving?

829
01:25:32,540 --> 01:25:35,050
If I were you, I wouldn't 
ask me that question.

830
01:25:36,210 --> 01:25:37,550
I would ask him.

831
01:25:38,380 --> 01:25:42,050
- Why? 
- He's the one who believes in miracles.

832
01:25:49,350 --> 01:25:51,900
There. Those mountains.

833
01:25:52,810 --> 01:25:54,610
That's it.

834
01:25:57,990 --> 01:25:59,900
- Do you see what's out there? 
- Yes.

835
01:26:00,400 --> 01:26:03,070
If you tell me we'll make it, 
I'll believe you.

836
01:26:03,200 --> 01:26:04,910
We'll make it.

837
01:26:07,910 --> 01:26:09,580
We have to.

838
01:27:22,900 --> 01:27:24,610
Sentinels.

839
01:27:35,960 --> 01:27:36,420
There's too many!

840
01:27:54,020 --> 01:27:55,350
Gotcha!

841
01:27:56,020 --> 01:27:58,190
- I need help here! 
- I can't beat them.

842
01:27:58,440 --> 01:28:00,860
- What do we do? 
- Go up, over them.

843
01:28:01,110 --> 01:28:04,070
- What? 
- The sky! It's the only way.

844
01:28:06,030 --> 01:28:07,780
Then up we go.

845
01:28:43,070 --> 01:28:44,900
Beautiful.

846
01:29:06,760 --> 01:29:09,430
Pump the igniter. The ship will start.

847
01:29:16,850 --> 01:29:19,270
Again. Slowly.

848
01:29:22,270 --> 01:29:23,770
Now!

849
01:29:49,260 --> 01:29:50,760
Trin?

850
01:29:52,800 --> 01:29:54,640
Trinity?

851
01:29:55,720 --> 01:29:57,350
Trinity?

852
01:29:58,560 --> 01:30:00,640
- I'm here. 
- Where?

853
01:30:00,770 --> 01:30:02,150
Here.

854
01:30:12,450 --> 01:30:13,820
We made it.

855
01:30:15,580 --> 01:30:17,370
You said we would.

856
01:30:19,660 --> 01:30:22,170
It's unbelievable, Trin.

857
01:30:23,170 --> 01:30:24,840
Light everywhere.

858
01:30:25,170 --> 01:30:28,000
Like the whole thing was built of light.

859
01:30:28,670 --> 01:30:30,800
I wish you could see what I see.

860
01:30:32,470 --> 01:30:34,510
You've already shown me so much.

861
01:30:36,760 --> 01:30:40,060
What is it, Trinity? 
What's wrong?

862
01:30:41,480 --> 01:30:43,940
I can't go with you, Neo.

863
01:30:45,650 --> 01:30:47,400
I've gone as far as I can.

864
01:30:47,690 --> 01:30:49,070
What?

865
01:30:52,030 --> 01:30:53,490
Oh, no.

866
01:30:54,360 --> 01:30:56,070
Oh, no. No, no.

867
01:30:56,870 --> 01:30:58,540
It's all right.

868
01:30:59,870 --> 01:31:01,540
It's time.

869
01:31:03,120 --> 01:31:05,580
I've done all that I could do.

870
01:31:06,840 --> 01:31:09,210
Now you have to do the rest.

871
01:31:09,960 --> 01:31:12,050
You have to finish it.

872
01:31:12,380 --> 01:31:14,550
You have to save Zion.

873
01:31:15,050 --> 01:31:16,680
I can't.

874
01:31:17,180 --> 01:31:20,520
- Not without you. 
- Yes, you can.

875
01:31:21,060 --> 01:31:22,730
You will.

876
01:31:23,730 --> 01:31:26,900
I believe it. I always have.

877
01:31:29,360 --> 01:31:30,980
Trinity.

878
01:31:33,240 --> 01:31:36,700
Trinity, you can't die.

879
01:31:38,740 --> 01:31:40,870
You can't.

880
01:31:41,160 --> 01:31:42,750
You can't.

881
01:31:42,910 --> 01:31:45,080
Yes, I can.

882
01:31:48,250 --> 01:31:50,630
You brought me back once.

883
01:31:52,880 --> 01:31:54,930
But not this time.

884
01:32:00,850 --> 01:32:02,770
Do you remember...

885
01:32:04,560 --> 01:32:07,440
...on that roof, after you caught me...

886
01:32:09,060 --> 01:32:10,820
...the last thing I said to you?

887
01:32:13,570 --> 01:32:15,110
You said, "I'm sorry."

888
01:32:16,450 --> 01:32:18,530
I wish I hadn't.

889
01:32:21,620 --> 01:32:23,910
That was my last thought.

890
01:32:26,290 --> 01:32:29,130
I wished I had one more chance...

891
01:32:30,040 --> 01:32:32,300
...to say what really mattered.

892
01:32:34,880 --> 01:32:37,680
To say how much I loved you.

893
01:32:40,100 --> 01:32:43,470
How grateful I was for every moment 
I was with you.

894
01:32:46,270 --> 01:32:51,190
But by the time I knew how to say 
what I wanted to, it was too late.

895
01:32:57,280 --> 01:32:59,820
But you brought me back.

896
01:33:02,740 --> 01:33:04,120
You gave me my wish.

897
01:33:08,290 --> 01:33:12,340
One more chance to say 
what I really wanted to say.

898
01:33:17,010 --> 01:33:18,840
Kiss me.

899
01:33:21,850 --> 01:33:23,640
Once more...

900
01:33:25,350 --> 01:33:26,730
...kiss me.

901
01:33:54,130 --> 01:33:56,210
Get that ammunition where it belongs!

902
01:33:56,340 --> 01:33:58,210
You got one chance to get this right.

903
01:33:58,880 --> 01:34:00,720
Get that damn thing mounted!

904
01:34:05,720 --> 01:34:08,270
- Hurry. 
- Let's go, let's go, let's go!

905
01:34:23,160 --> 01:34:24,490
Neo...

906
01:34:24,820 --> 01:34:27,240
...if you're gonna do something, 
do it quick.

907
01:36:36,040 --> 01:36:38,080
I only ask to say 
what I've come to say.

908
01:36:38,290 --> 01:36:42,090
After that, do what you want, 
and I won't try and stop you.

909
01:36:46,220 --> 01:36:47,550
Speak.

910
01:36:48,340 --> 01:36:51,260
The program Smith has grown 
beyond your control.

911
01:36:51,470 --> 01:36:54,890
Soon he will spread through this city 
as he spread through the Matrix.

912
01:36:55,060 --> 01:36:56,390
You cannot stop him.

913
01:36:58,480 --> 01:37:00,770
- But I can. 
- We don't need you!

914
01:37:01,820 --> 01:37:04,110
We need nothing!

915
01:37:05,240 --> 01:37:09,110
If that's true, then I've made a mistake, 
and you should kill me now.

916
01:37:14,240 --> 01:37:16,080
What do you want?

917
01:37:17,500 --> 01:37:18,750
Peace.

918
01:37:44,610 --> 01:37:46,480
What are they doing?

919
01:37:52,120 --> 01:37:54,120
What are you doing?

920
01:37:57,290 --> 01:37:59,160
Morpheus!

921
01:38:23,560 --> 01:38:25,520
And if you fail?

922
01:38:27,820 --> 01:38:29,780
I won't.

923
01:38:51,260 --> 01:38:52,840
Neo.

924
01:38:52,970 --> 01:38:54,590
He fights for us.

925
01:39:36,390 --> 01:39:39,260
Mr. Anderson, welcome back.

926
01:39:39,470 --> 01:39:41,600
We missed you.

927
01:39:45,730 --> 01:39:48,610
You like what I've done with the place?

928
01:39:49,230 --> 01:39:50,900
It ends tonight.

929
01:39:51,900 --> 01:39:54,900
I know it does. I've seen it.

930
01:39:55,070 --> 01:39:58,780
That's why the rest of me 
is just going to enjoy the show...

931
01:39:58,990 --> 01:40:02,620
...because we already know 
that I'm the one that beats you.

932
01:41:54,940 --> 01:41:57,820
Can you feel it, Mr. Anderson...

933
01:41:58,030 --> 01:42:00,400
...closing in on you?

934
01:42:00,610 --> 01:42:02,740
Oh, I can.

935
01:42:04,120 --> 01:42:08,200
I really should thank you for it. 
After all, it was your life...

936
01:42:08,370 --> 01:42:12,040
...that taught me the purpose of all life.

937
01:42:12,460 --> 01:42:15,920
The purpose of life is to end.

938
01:45:51,840 --> 01:45:53,760
Why, Mr. Anderson?

939
01:45:53,890 --> 01:45:57,770
Why, why, why?

940
01:45:57,930 --> 01:45:59,270
Why do you do it?

941
01:46:00,020 --> 01:46:01,980
Why? Why get up?

942
01:46:02,190 --> 01:46:03,980
Why keep fighting?

943
01:46:05,520 --> 01:46:07,990
Do you believe you're fighting 
for something?

944
01:46:08,190 --> 01:46:10,820
For more than your survival?

945
01:46:11,030 --> 01:46:14,280
Can you tell me what it is? 
Do you even know?

946
01:46:17,790 --> 01:46:19,500
Is it freedom or truth?

947
01:46:19,710 --> 01:46:22,040
Perhaps peace? Could it be for love?

948
01:46:22,250 --> 01:46:25,630
Illusions, Mr. Anderson. 
Vagaries of perception.

949
01:46:26,050 --> 01:46:29,130
Temporary constructs 
of a feeble human intellect...

950
01:46:29,300 --> 01:46:31,880
...trying desperately 
to justify an existence...

951
01:46:32,090 --> 01:46:34,140
...that is without meaning or purpose!

952
01:46:34,300 --> 01:46:37,770
And all of them as artificial 
as the Matrix itself...

953
01:46:37,930 --> 01:46:44,020
...although only a human mind could 
invent something as insipid as love.

954
01:46:46,570 --> 01:46:48,650
You must be able to see it, 
Mr. Anderson.

955
01:46:48,820 --> 01:46:53,360
You must know it by now. You can't 
win. It's pointless to keep fighting.

956
01:46:56,160 --> 01:46:59,370
Why, Mr. Anderson, why? 
Why do you persist?

957
01:47:02,670 --> 01:47:04,880
Because I choose to.

958
01:48:09,860 --> 01:48:12,900
This is my world! My world!

959
01:48:37,590 --> 01:48:39,300
Wait.

960
01:48:39,510 --> 01:48:41,640
I've seen this.

961
01:48:42,850 --> 01:48:45,140
This is it. This is the end.

962
01:48:46,850 --> 01:48:50,770
Yes. You were laying right there, 
just like that.

963
01:48:50,900 --> 01:48:53,280
And I... I...

964
01:48:53,440 --> 01:48:59,280
I stand here, right here, 
and I'm supposed to say something.

965
01:49:01,280 --> 01:49:04,790
"Everything that has a beginning 
has an end, Neo."

966
01:49:13,550 --> 01:49:17,260
What? What did I just say?

967
01:49:22,640 --> 01:49:26,480
No, no. This isn't right. 
This can't be right.

968
01:49:33,980 --> 01:49:35,650
Get away from me!

969
01:49:35,820 --> 01:49:37,190
What are you afraid of?

970
01:49:37,990 --> 01:49:39,320
It's a trick.

971
01:49:39,990 --> 01:49:42,200
You were right, Smith.

972
01:49:43,160 --> 01:49:44,990
You were always right.

973
01:49:48,290 --> 01:49:50,000
It was inevitable.

974
01:50:21,780 --> 01:50:23,370
Is it over?

975
01:50:54,400 --> 01:50:56,730
Oh, no, no, no.

976
01:50:56,900 --> 01:50:58,440
No, it's not fair.

977
01:51:52,790 --> 01:51:55,120
It is done.

978
01:52:27,070 --> 01:52:29,370
It doesn't make sense.

979
01:52:33,330 --> 01:52:34,080
He did it.

980
01:52:35,750 --> 01:52:37,960
He saved us.

981
01:52:38,250 --> 01:52:40,380
He saved us.

982
01:52:41,000 --> 01:52:44,210
It's over! He did it! He did it!

983
01:52:44,510 --> 01:52:45,840
He did it! It's over!

984
01:52:46,010 --> 01:52:48,470
It's over! He did it! He did it!

985
01:52:48,680 --> 01:52:50,260
- What is it? What happened?

986
01:52:50,260 --> 01:52:51,220
- Sir, he ended the war.

987
01:52:51,430 --> 01:52:53,310
The machines, they're gone.

988
01:52:53,520 --> 01:52:56,810
The war is over, sir. The war is over.

989
01:52:58,440 --> 01:53:01,820
Zion! Zion!

990
01:53:02,020 --> 01:53:03,690
Zion, it's over!

991
01:53:04,110 --> 01:53:05,610
It's over!

992
01:53:05,780 --> 01:53:08,450
The war is over!

993
01:53:08,570 --> 01:53:11,450
The war is over!

994
01:53:11,620 --> 01:53:14,120
Whoo!

995
01:53:32,760 --> 01:53:35,680
I have imagined this moment...

996
01:53:36,230 --> 01:53:38,480
...for so long.

997
01:53:42,400 --> 01:53:44,150
Is this real?

998
01:53:52,990 --> 01:53:55,830
Neo, wherever you are...

999
01:53:56,830 --> 01:53:58,870
...thank you.

1000
01:54:42,710 --> 01:54:44,040
Good morning.

1001
01:55:05,310 --> 01:55:09,190
Well, now. Ain't this a surprise.

1002
01:55:09,650 --> 01:55:11,780
You played a very dangerous game.

1003
01:55:11,990 --> 01:55:14,240
Change always is.

1004
01:55:14,820 --> 01:55:18,120
Just how long do you think 
this peace is going to last?

1005
01:55:19,490 --> 01:55:20,830
As long as it can.

1006
01:55:25,000 --> 01:55:26,960
What about the others?

1007
01:55:28,670 --> 01:55:30,090
What others?

1008
01:55:30,260 --> 01:55:31,880
The ones that want out.

1009
01:55:32,670 --> 01:55:34,760
Obviously, they will be freed.

1010
01:55:35,340 --> 01:55:36,970
I have your word?

1011
01:55:37,180 --> 01:55:40,930
What do you think I am? Human?

1012
01:55:54,950 --> 01:55:56,490
Oracle!

1013
01:56:03,370 --> 01:56:05,500
We were afraid we might not find you.

1014
01:56:05,710 --> 01:56:08,340
Everything's okay now.

1015
01:56:08,880 --> 01:56:10,630
Look, look.

1016
01:56:11,210 --> 01:56:13,630
Just look at that.

1017
01:56:14,300 --> 01:56:16,970
Beautiful.

1018
01:56:17,890 --> 01:56:20,310
Did you do that?

1019
01:56:20,640 --> 01:56:22,810
For Neo.

1020
01:56:23,140 --> 01:56:25,100
That's nice.

1021
01:56:25,310 --> 01:56:26,980
I know he'd love it.

1022
01:56:27,650 --> 01:56:29,650
Will we ever see him again?

1023
01:56:30,230 --> 01:56:32,940
I suspect so.

1024
01:56:33,150 --> 01:56:34,820
Someday.

1025
01:56:39,660 --> 01:56:41,450
Did you always know?

1026
01:56:41,620 --> 01:56:44,870
Oh, no. No, I didn't.

1027
01:56:45,410 --> 01:56:48,000
But I believed.

1028
01:56:48,920 --> 01:56:51,340
I believed.
